type: dataset
keywords:
  - Hodge conjecture
  - Fermat curves
  - gamma normalization
  - Riemann relations
  - polarization
  - K3 surfaces
  - Klein quartic
  - cyclotomic levels
  - computational verification
  - Lean 4
abstract: >-
  A unified research program built on the dynamic principle: geometry
  supplies only the integer triple (n, B, lambda_0); a universal
  parameter-free pipeline constructs spin phases (pi/N), braking
  (delta^4/k), effective corrections, and full period normalizations.
  The ladder of stands spans the torus (4, 1, 4*pi^2), the Fermat
  quartic K3 (Neron-Severi rank 20), the Klein quartic Jacobian
  (j = -3375), and the cyclotomic levels N = 15/30 (genera 91 and 406)
  with a closed system of eight lemmas and six theorems. Certificates
  A-H cover cycle certification, period-based kernel closure,
  mu_4-equivariance, flow termination with exact time, rationalization
  with a priori denominator bounds, Hodge lattice indices with the
  Chowla-Selberg layer, and the full Gross gamma-normalization
  (volume 1125 = sqrt(3^4 * 5^6)). The protocol V1-V9 is fully
  reproducible; verification runs in Python, Julia, Fortran, C, Rust,
  and the Lean 4 kernel.
